<title>UK: Baltic, Black Sea exports fall 36,149 bpd on week.</title>
<headline>Baltic, Black Sea exports fall 36,149 bpd on week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals fell 36,149 barrels per day (bpd) in the fourth week of March from the previous week to 1.85 million bpd, Petro-Logistics said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The total was 336,999 bpd higher than the same week last year.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports fell 40,641 bpd on the week to 0.98 million bpd, which is just below year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports rose 19,645 bpd to 580,728 bpd, which is 224,420 bpd above year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports rose 61,723 bpd to 273,896 bpd and were 173,426 bpd higher than in the same week last year.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics lists a breakdown in metric tonnes of petroleum exports from the Baltic and Black Sea in the third week of March.  </p>
<p>			 Crude	  Fuel    Gas Oil   Mogas/Jet  Total</p>
<p>FSU		    939,932    296,104   435,406    14,108   1,685,550</p>
<p>Romania/</p>
<p>Bulgaria		 --	   --	110,611	--	 110,611</p>
<p>TOTAL tonnes	 939,932    296,104   546,017    14,108   1,796,161</p>
<p>TOTAL bpd	    978,872    273,896   580,728    15,882   1,849,378</p>
<p>Change week bpd    -40,641    +61,723   +19,645   -76,876     -36,149</p>
<p>Change year bpd    -11,170   +173,426  +224,420   -25,209    +336,999</p>
